# Server-side secrets for the Netlify Functions. Copy to .env for local
# `netlify dev`; for the live site set the same names in the Netlify UI
# (Site configuration → Environment variables) — a .env file is never
# deployed. .env itself is gitignored; this example file is not.

# --- Password → key vending (/api/keys) -------------------------------
# Someone who types XPLAINER_PASSWORD into any key field in the editor's ⚙
# dialog gets the keys below instead. Set the password plus at least one
# key, or the endpoint stays off (503).
XPLAINER_PASSWORD=
XPLAINER_ANTHROPIC_KEY=
XPLAINER_GEMINI_KEY=
XPLAINER_OPENAI_KEY=

# Deliberately NOT named ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY / GEMINI_API_KEY:
# the Netlify AI Gateway injects those names (with matching *_BASE_URL vars)
# into /api/generate at runtime. Setting your own values under those names
# would pair a real key with the gateway's base URL and break that path.

# --- Built-in AI (/api/generate) --------------------------------------
# Needs no variables here at all — enable AI for the team in the Netlify UI
# and the gateway injects its own credentials.
